# Marineris: the first of the hard series, a roller coaster in a canyon. The start stands 80 m
# up on a summit mesa: a booster launches the car off its edge into a plunge of 48 m, over a
# camelback on red tube scaffolding, round a high banked sweeper and down to a chicane of 90°
# turns 16 m up, then a booster into the kicker: up to a second in the air and 13 m over the lip
# at 330 km/h, onto a landing hill that catches 145 to 378 km/h, down to the canyon floor. The east side is the lift hill: 48 m up, an S of 90° turns
# on the scaffolding (a fall is a respawn), a booster off the top into the longest drop. The
# south side rolls over two long camelbacks along the canyon wall, a booster climbs 24 m to a
# last 90° turn at height, and a booster sends the car up a butte to the finish.
#
# Every vertical curve is wide enough for the speeds it is taken at (a crest under
# v² / 40 m/s² launches the car, a tight sag crushes it): the drops and climbs are 5 to 8 cells
# long; only the first plunge, taken slowly, is steep. Boosters relaunch the car after the slow
# turns, and into the kicker, with no climb before it (a sag then a crest, at 300 km/h, throws
# the car as its springs rebound). About 46 s for the braking autopilot, 44 s for a player flat
# out.
name Marineris
seed 4207
# 2: the north side only drops to 16 m, its chicane and kicker up there, the kicker straight
# after the booster with an 8-cell landing hill: taken flat out through the chicane and boosted
# (330 km/h), the climb before the kicker threw the car onto it.
version 2
start 0 -8 10 0
straight booster
slope5_down6
slope3_up2
slope3_down2
banked3_right
slope6_down2
checkpoint
straight
turn1_right
turn1_left
